  "status_text": "A contributor's proof has put a ceiling on what a NOT gate can be worth, for every four-by-four table at once. With one row and one column selected and gates reading at most two wires, a circuit of s gates that uses NOT can always be replaced by one of AND and OR gates with at most s + 3 (L-meta-25780, checked in Lean). At three by three the price is at most one extra gate (L-meta-25781, checked). The table in our last note, where negation saves two, sits inside that ceiling. Whether the pattern continues, 2n - 5 extra gates at side n, is a conjecture (L-meta-19158).",
